        "original_id": "a5ed722c-9805-5641-96e7-9f37e844b0b1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Gonzales v. Carhart; Lawrence v. Texas\n- Organizations: United States Supreme Court\n- Laws: Partial-Birth Abortion Ban Act of 2003; Texas sodomy law; sodomy laws in 13 other states\n- Topics: abortion law; same-sex sexual activity rights\n\nFacts:\n- In 2003, Lawrence v. Texas, 539 U.S. 558, was decided by the United States Supreme Court.\n- In 2003, the United States Supreme Court struck down the Texas sodomy law in Lawrence v. Texas by a 6–3 vote.\n- In 2003, Lawrence v. Texas invalidated sodomy laws in 13 other states and made same-sex sexual activity legal in every U.S. state and territory.\n- In 2007, Gonzales v. Carhart, 550 U.S. 124, was a United States Supreme Court case that upheld the Partial-Birth Abortion Ban Act of 2003.",
